WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.595 --> 00:00:10.294
Priya Raman: Hi Heather, hi Megan. How's the week going over there?

2
00:00:10.913 --> 00:00:18.273
Heather Collins: Busy. We have two offices short a front desk person, so everyone's covering phones more than usual.

3
00:00:18.655 --> 00:00:26.527
Megan Foster: Yeah, Kelly's been out at the Meridian practice all week training the new hire, so it's been a scramble.

4
00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:32.569
Priya Raman: That's a lot. Did anything about call handling change while people were covering?

5
00:00:33.008 --> 00:00:39.885
Heather Collins: A little. We told them to lean on the summaries since they're not used to the new-patient script.

6
00:00:41.266 --> 00:00:45.481
Megan Foster: The managers still read them every morning. That part hasn't changed.

7
00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:54.635
Priya Raman: Good. What are you seeing volume-wise? Last time we talked you were around eight thousand calls a month.

8
00:00:54.852 --> 00:01:00.167
Megan Foster: We're at about eighty-three hundred for September. New-patient calls are up maybe six percent.

9
00:01:00.542 --> 00:01:05.832
Priya Raman: Nice. And the Google Ads side is still doing the heavy lifting for those?

10
00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:14.513
Megan Foster: It is. We've got fourteen campaigns running across the practices, mostly new patient and a couple for implants.

11
00:01:15.957 --> 00:01:23.638
Priya Raman: Okay, so the reason I wanted to check in. Anything come up since August that's worth putting on my list?

12
00:01:24.546 --> 00:01:33.717
Heather Collins: There's one thing. I had lunch with a peer at another group last week and she was going on about CallRail.

13
00:01:34.726 --> 00:01:36.706
Priya Raman: What was she saying about it?

14
00:01:37.218 --> 00:01:44.974
Heather Collins: That their calls land in Google Ads the same day, and she was pretty sure their quote came in under what we pay.

15
00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:54.291
Megan Foster: She also said the setup was quicker, but I don't know how much of that is just her being her.

16
00:01:54.986 --> 00:02:02.039
Heather Collins: Right. I'm not looking to rip anything out, but when someone hands you a lower number it makes you ask.

17
00:02:03.528 --> 00:02:09.457
Priya Raman: That's fair. Can I ask what your sync timing looks like now on your end?

18
00:02:10.621 --> 00:02:19.366
Megan Foster: I usually see the conversions in Google Ads a few hours after the calls. Sometimes the next morning if it's a late call.

19
00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:23.451
Priya Raman: And that timing matters because of Smart Bidding?

20
00:02:24.726 --> 00:02:34.549
Megan Foster: It does. If a call comes in Thursday night and the bid data doesn't show up until Friday, we're a day behind on the weekend push.

21
00:02:35.124 --> 00:02:42.091
Heather Collins: Especially for the implant campaigns. Those are expensive clicks and we want the signal in fast.

22
00:02:43.475 --> 00:02:54.842
Priya Raman: Got it. I don't want to guess at what's driving the timing, so let me take that back and get you a real answer instead of me speculating.

23
00:02:56.278 --> 00:03:01.051
Heather Collins: That works. I'd rather hear it straight than have you promise something.

24
00:03:02.336 --> 00:03:12.677
Priya Raman: I'll follow up by early next week. Is there anything on the Meta side you want me to look at while I'm in there?

25
00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.678
Megan Foster: Meta's fine. We're barely spending there this quarter, so no rush.

26
00:03:19.559 --> 00:03:21.393
Priya Raman: Okay. Anything else on operations?

27
00:03:22.653 --> 00:03:27.937
Heather Collins: We're opening the Nampa office in January, so we'll need tracking numbers set up before that.

28
00:03:28.172 --> 00:03:31.319
Priya Raman: How many lines are you thinking for that one?

29
00:03:31.827 --> 00:03:36.261
Heather Collins: Probably three to start. Front desk, hygiene, and one for the new-patient line.

30
00:03:36.628 --> 00:03:43.500
Priya Raman: I'll put a note in for December so we're not doing it the week you open.

31
00:03:44.822 --> 00:03:48.503
Megan Foster: Please. That's how the last one went and it was chaos.

32
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.086
Priya Raman: Understood. Anything on the summaries themselves?

33
00:03:53.263 --> 00:03:55.653
Megan Foster: They're fine. Managers use them, no complaints.

34
00:03:55.999 --> 00:04:02.676
Priya Raman: Good. I'll send you a short recap today with the follow-up date and the Nampa note.

35
00:04:03.736 --> 00:04:07.159
Heather Collins: Sounds good, Priya. Thanks for listening on the CallRail thing.

36
00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.250
Priya Raman: Of course. Talk soon.

37
00:04:10.225 --> 00:04:11.025
Megan Foster: Bye.
